{"version":1,"content":"<html><body><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://pro-img-cdn.tvb.com/uploads/image/2026/10/2026npZgCU4xcx1792832472.jpg?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1200\"/><p>不少長者隨年紀漸長，肌肉量下降、身體功能退化，即患肌少症。有機構篩查發現一成受訪長者跌倒風險高。</p><p></p><p>聖方濟各大學與物理治療師協會等，為200名長者就肌少症做評估，發現兩成三肌肉流失率較高，有潛在肌少症風險，一成一較高風險跌倒。</p><p></p><p><br/> <p><br/> <img alt=\"Picture_J.MUSCLE-1530.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://pro-img-cdn.tvb.com/uploads/image/2026/10/2026LsZCUpIjAi1792832481.jpg?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1200\"/><br/> </p><br/></p><p></p><p>團隊指，不少長者誤以為步態不穩、雙腳無力，或偶然跌倒、絆倒，是正常年老現象，無及早求醫，錯過黃金復康期，認為社區基層網絡必須主動干預，建議長者做針對阻力和平衡訓練，攝取高品質蛋白質和維生素D，提升肌肉量。</p></body></html>","scraped_at":"2026-10-24T11:54:43.146332+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":215,"images":2,"source":"TVB 新聞","fallback":"none","origin":"article-html","completeness":"extracted"},"published_at":"2026-10-24T08:14:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-24T20:38:02.141803+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-10-24T11:51:15.054935+00:00","content_hash":"8da8bda47bafa890659695cc461159ea31c80d0919d6d2a7051ea74c7e9cf5e3","evidence_status":"full","scrape_error":null,"content_retention":null,"content_capture":null}